{
  "story": "sc-19542",
  "epic": 17137,
  "description": "Per-(family, backend) rung-4 prerequisite records, derived from the pinned inference revision by scripts/rung4-contract-prerequisites.mjs. `additionalPrerequisites` is what that provider appends through `MemoryProviderContract::additional_prerequisites` for `MemoryStrategy::BoundedTransformerResidency`; the shared edge every provider carries regardless lives in the generator as SHARED_RUNG4_PREREQUISITES, mirroring gen-core BOUNDED_TRANSFORMER_RESIDENCY_REQUIRES. `conditional` is true when the construction appending the edge is not in every production build — a `then_some` on a runtime condition (mlx-gen-anima, mlx-gen-krea) or a `#[cfg]`-gated contract function (candle-gen-z-image, candle-gen-lens and candle-gen-krea are `#[cfg(any(feature = \"cuda\", test))]`). It is also true for a filtered list (`[A, B, C].into_iter().filter(..).map(..)`, candle-gen-sana), where the listed strategies are a ceiling the predicate narrows rather than a declaration; the extractor does not read the predicate, so it marks the whole list. The gate evaluates a conditional edge as PRESENT, because for an admission gate \"this provider may demand rung 1\" is the fail-closed reading. `stagedResidencySupport` is the provider's own MemoryStrategySupport for the rung those edges name, needed because gen-core validate_selection satisfies an EngagedInSameRequest edge VACUOUSLY when the prerequisite rung is StructurallyNotApplicable; null means the extractor could not read one declaration for the crate, and null falls through to the engagement term rather than admitting.",
  "inferenceRevision": "dbe0d8715fca678fe4126188d6d04bfd19146455",
