  "granularity": "One record per (FAMILY, backend), which is coarser than the contracts it summarises, and the join is a UNION over the crate. Two limits follow, both live at the pinned revision. (1) Several catalog families share one inference crate — FLUX.2 klein and FLUX.2 dev are both candle-gen-flux2/mlx-gen-flux2 — so those families cannot hold different edge sets even if the crate declares different ones per entry. (2) One crate may declare several contract VARIANTS: candle-gen-krea/src/lib.rs builds krea_2_turbo at :1396 with the rung-4 edge and krea_2_turbo_control at :1700 without it, and the record carries the union, so the base variant's edge is attributed to the whole family. Today that over-attribution decides nothing — the control variant declares rung 4 StructurallyNotApplicable, so its cells never reach the prerequisite check — but it is an over-count and not a fact about the control provider. Splitting the key by variant is what would fix it, and no consumer needs that yet."
}
